Original-generation public ESP32 runtime boundary for OpenRigCue Rust firmware

The application, String ownership, protocols, device control and callback
logic remain Rust. This crate binds the independently published original
C/FreeRTOS/NimBLE substrate. It does not extract or execute SRS application
code. No original firmware image is copied into the resulting application.

Pinned redistributable substrate:
- espressif/arduino-esp32 release 1.0.6, tools/sdk: IDF
  v3.3.5-1-g85c43024c. Official release archive, SHA256 in
  ../tools/esp32-runtime.sh. The archive includes original SDK library code,
  headers, linker scripts and original-generation public bootloaders.
  https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/releases/tag/1.0.6
- Espressif Xtensa GCC5.2.0, 1.22.0-97-gc752ad5. Official archive and SHA256
  in ../tools/esp32-runtime.sh. Runtime library use is covered by the GCC
  Runtime Library Exception. The compiler itself is not redistributed.
- h2zero/NimBLE-Arduino 1.3.1, commit
  725079ade938d5e0f4de16695ba2b9039f5ffeb8. Only the original C host and
  transport substrate is compiled. Original C++ application-facing classes
  are implemented in the OpenRigCue Rust source.
  https://github.com/h2zero/NimBLE-Arduino/tree/725079ade938d5e0f4de16695ba2b9039f5ffeb8

Unmodified license and notice texts are retained under licenses/. SDK and
NimBLE sources preserve their own additional source-level copyright notices.
The private build prepends #line directives to the NimBLE C copies solely to
retain source diagnostic __FILE__ strings; it changes no C implementation.
